// AAC rule-program executor (PLAN-1046 T-02): Auto port of
// `ace_syntax_runtime::parse` — explicit work stacks (no native recursion),
// config-driven Pratt, declaration-level recovery, budgets, failure memo,
// and copy-adopted grafting.
//
// Faithful port notes:
//   * ordered-choice backtracking: alt failure restores the alt-entry save
//     and clears partial children; cut steps (PLAN-927) freeze backtracking
//     below the commit depth;
//   * List steps consume `sep` tokens between items; a clean item failure
//     ends the list; the ROOT-level list skips garbage as error leaves;
//   * Pratt frames stage WantPrimary/WantOp/WantArgs/WantClose/Done with
//     per-frame operand/op stacks in shared arenas;
//   * declaration-level recovery (sync ∪ first(rule)) rebuilds leading
//     trivia, eats error leaves to the stop point, and produces a MISSING
//     placeholder with the expected rule kind;
//   * node spans are built ABSOLUTE and relativized at declaration
//     boundaries (origin = cover start incl. leading trivia);
//   * the failure memo keys (rule, token pos, same-line latch, bracket)
//     exactly and only replays total failures (bounded, best-effort —
//     clearing loses speed, never results);
//   * grafting adopts an unchanged old declaration by COPYING its node
//     range (relative spans verbatim, decl field remapped to the new tree
//     decl index) and skipping its tokens — the Rc block sharing on the
//     Rust side is a storage optimization with no observable here.
//
// Machine state is passed as parallel flat lists in a fixed order:
//   pg (program arena), cs (scanner buckets), firsts/nullable (FirstSets),
//   toks (5/token), t/ef/decls (CST arenas), mc (scalar cursor state),
//   pending (trivia token indices), fr (frame arena, stride 40), saves,
//   pvals/pops/optriv (pratt arenas), arule/ai (active rules),
//   hd/hs/he/hm (hints), dm/ds/de (tree diags), fm (failure memo),
//   ot/oef/odecls/gcand/gshift/ginfo (graft input; ginfo[0] = active).

